# Cloudflare static-asset redirects.
#
# The CME article shipped briefly at /guides/cme-money/ and that URL went into a sitemap
# that had already been submitted to Search Console. It was renamed to /how-to/ because
# "guide" reads as a travel guide rather than a how-to. Redirecting rather than leaving a
# 404 keeps any crawl signal and stops Search Console reporting a dead sitemap URL.
/guides/cme-money/  /how-to/deduct-cme-travel/  301
/guides/            /how-to/deduct-cme-travel/  301
/guides/*           /how-to/deduct-cme-travel/  301

# The Oct 2026 discovery pass normalised two split country spellings in conferences.js
# ("United Kingdom" -> "UK", "Czechia" -> "Czech Republic") because each pair was building
# two hub pages for one country, and /city/glasgow/ collided between them. build-hubs.js
# then correctly pruned the now-empty hubs — but both were already in a submitted sitemap,
# so without these they are dead indexed URLs rather than consolidated ones.
/country/united-kingdom/  /country/uk/              301
/country/czechia/         /country/czech-republic/   301

